{"duration_api_ms":347171,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8919400c-1e22-40db-a844-79bf7fa443f8","total_cost_usd":0.376074,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12460,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":32623,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":25715},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12460,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":32623,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12460,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12460},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":32623,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12460,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.376074,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":25715,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"No feasible design exists yet: 11 of 20 evaluations were geometry failures, and the rest fail max_g (limit 12 g), heatshield mass fraction, or both. All 11 geometry failures fit one rule: fore-cone length = D*(0.5 - 0.1*(1-cos(theta)) - b*cos(theta))/tan(theta), which must be >= 0. This reproduces the reported lengths for C-d03a6d571826, C-e0d635fd334b and C-c28d2aecc04e, so high bluntness needs a high cone angle. The feasible window looks like: flight-path angle no steeper than about -3.3 deg (g <= 12), diameter no larger than about 3.0 m (mass fraction), and a high cone angle with the largest bluntness the geometry allows. The hypervolume reference is 450 K in temperature, so bondline temperature dominates the hypervolume: one Kelvin is worth far more than tens of kW/m2 of heat flux. The proposals therefore cluster near the g and mass limits, with a few shallower or smaller probes for trade-off coverage.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-e0059024652c: gamma -2.69 gives g 10.56 (margin 0.1201, so the g limit is 12). C-316c5e108e1a: gamma -3.40 gives g 11.97 (margin 0.002). Steeper entries fail g: C-9b459669aa7c gives 12.9 at -3.52 and C-029296252ff3 gives 13.6 at -4.41.\",\"Mass-fraction margin falls with diameter: C-a6b969cef0a0 at D 3.07 gives +0.008, C-e0059024652c at 3.39 gives -0.128, C-029296252ff3 at 3.63 gives -0.19, C-316c5e108e1a at 4.30 gives -0.83. Small diameters pass easily, for example 0.83 at D 1.24 in C-9b459669aa7c. The diameter ceiling is therefore about 3.0 m.\",\"Peak heat flux q roughly follows q^2 = K*sin(gamma)/(b*D^3), with K about 5e13 at theta 42-49 and about 3.2-3.6e13 at theta 55-65, fitted across the 9 valid rows. Higher cone angle, larger D and larger bluntness therefore all lower q and the heat load.\",\"Bondline temperature rises with heat-load proxy Q = q/sin(gamma), roughly dT = 76 + 3.9*Q[MW/m2]. Examples: C-316c5e108e1a has Q 4.8 and T 393; C-9b459669aa7c has Q 28 and T 484. Shallow entry adds a few K (C-e0059024652c is about +9 K above trend at -2.69 deg).\",\"Geometry-failure rows C-c28d2aecc04e, C-69ef29176b15 and C-5a78f6504d22 all combine bluntness above 0.96 with theta at or below 53 deg. Valid rows with b*cos(theta) below about 0.48 all built.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak heating scales roughly with sqrt(rho/Rn)*V^3 (Sutton-Graves, prior knowledge). It falls with larger nose radius (Rn = b*D) and with lower ballistic coefficient (larger D and higher-drag blunt, high-angle cones). Bondline temperature follows integrated heat load, which falls with the same levers and rises as the entry gets shallower and the heating pulse lengthens. Peak deceleration is set mainly by entry angle, plus a small bump for small, high-ballistic-coefficient bodies. The best region is therefore large D within the mass limit, theta 62-70 deg, b near the geometry ceiling b <= (0.4 - margin)/cos(theta) + 0.1, and gamma near -3.1 to -3.3 deg. Shallower gamma trades higher T for lower q.\",\"uncertainty\":\"Diameter and gamma are extrapolated: the mass-fraction dependence on theta and b is unmeasured, and the 3.0 m ceiling comes from only three rows. g for large-D, high-drag blunt shapes at gamma -3.2 to -3.4 sits within about 0.4 g of the limit, so several proposals may fail g. K(theta) and the T-vs-Q fit come from 9 points with confounded variables. Predicted temperatures below 393 K are extrapolation. The 0.02-0.09 geometry margins are computed from the fitted rule and should be safe, but a minimum cone length may exist that the data does not show.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-a6b969cef0a0\",\"rationale\":\"Anchor design: the mass-feasible D near 3.0 (C-a6b969cef0a0 passed mass at 3.07), with high cone angle and large bluntness to cut q and heat load, at gamma -3.2 for g margin. Geometry margin g_geom = 0.082.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.95,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":264000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Most likely first feasible point; tests the whole high-theta, high-bluntness hypothesis.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-029296252ff3\",\"rationale\":\"Push toward the g limit (gamma -3.3) with slightly smaller D 2.9 for mass margin, theta 66 and b 1.0 (geometry margin 0.034).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.9,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes how close gamma can go to the g limit for a moderate-D blunt shape.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1c570e52d539\",\"rationale\":\"Mid-high theta 62 with b 0.87 (geometry margin 0.039) at D 2.8; checks whether less extreme bluntness costs much T.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.8,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.87,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":62.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.15},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":313000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the middle of the trade-off and tests the theta dependence of K.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e0059024652c\",\"rationale\":\"C-e0059024652c only failed mass (D 3.39) and had g margin 0.12. Reduce D to 3.0, raise theta to 55 and b to 0.72 (geometry margin 0.044), and steepen gamma to -3.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.72,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":55.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":324000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Direct repair of the nearest-feasible row; gives a lower-theta reference for the mass and T trend.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-316c5e108e1a\",\"rationale\":\"C-316c5e108e1a met g and T but failed mass at D 4.3. Shrink to D 3.0 at theta 48, b 0.6 (geometry margin 0.065) to isolate the low-theta branch.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.6,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":48.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":396000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":407,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether low cone angle has a mass-fraction or g penalty versus high-theta designs.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a6b969cef0a0\",\"rationale\":\"Push the extremes: D 3.05, theta 70, b 1.1 (geometry margin 0.058) at gamma -3.25. Expected best-T corner if the mass fraction holds.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.05,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":241000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Sets the lower bound of achievable T and q and probes the mass limit at the largest D tried.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-029296252ff3\",\"rationale\":\"Smaller D 2.6 with maximal bluntness at theta 70 (geometry margin 0.05) and gamma -3.3, to measure how much T is lost when diameter drops.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.6,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":309000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Quantifies the D-sensitivity of T and whether small-D g inflation breaks the g limit at -3.3 deg.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e0059024652c\",\"rationale\":\"D 2.4 with b 1.15 at theta 70 (geometry margin 0.041) and gamma -3.0; a low-mass, comfortable-g corner of the space.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.4,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":325000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the lower-D end of the trade-off and the model of q against D^-3 scaling.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-5f1fb1e8e97d\",\"rationale\":\"Shallower gamma -2.6 at D 2.9, theta 60, b 0.8 (geometry margin 0.05): lower q and g margin, higher T.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.9,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.8,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":60.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":285000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Maps the gamma trade-off (q down, T up) for front coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e0059024652c\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow-side coverage: D 3.0, theta 68, b 0.95 at gamma -2.2, aiming at low heat flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.95,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":219000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":412,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front toward low q; compare with the gamma -3.2 sibling to fit the gamma sensitivity of T.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e0059024652c\",\"rationale\":\"Very shallow gamma -2.0 with D 3.0, b 1.0, theta 68 (geometry margin 0.063) to see whether T grows steeply at shallow entry.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":203000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the shallow-angle T penalty, which is extrapolated from a single row (C-e0059024652c).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1c570e52d539\",\"rationale\":\"Moderate theta 57 with b 0.74 (geometry margin 0.052) at D 2.9, gamma -3.2; fills the theta 55-60 gap between the tested rows.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.9,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.74,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":57.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":338000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Interpolates theta and b within the safe geometry region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a6b969cef0a0\",\"rationale\":\"Test the g boundary directly: gamma -3.4 with D 3.0, theta 69, b 1.0 (geometry margin 0.077). The 316c row sat exactly at g = 11.97 at this angle.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":265000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393,\"feasible\":false},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the steepest allowable gamma for a moderate-D, high-drag blunt shape; the g limit is the main lever on T.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-316c5e108e1a\",\"rationale\":\"D 2.7, theta 64, b 0.9 (geometry margin 0.049), gamma -3.2: a mid-diameter, mid-bluntness point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.7,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":64.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":322000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds spread in D without leaving the likely-feasible region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-029296252ff3\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate theta 52, b 0.65 (geometry margin 0.062), D 2.95, gamma -3.0: a moderate-drag design for diversity in the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.95,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.65,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":52.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":363000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":407,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the mass fraction depends on theta at fixed D and refines K(theta).\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d13be3c7a739\",\"rationale\":\"Small-D probe D 2.2, theta 66, b 1.0 (geometry margin 0.034), gamma -3.0, to see the mass-fraction and g behaviour of small, high-ballistic-coefficient bodies.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.2,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":397000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Calibrates the small-D end of the q(D) and T(D) trends and the g inflation seen in C-9b459669aa7c.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-61fffdb55e9f\",\"rationale\":\"Maximum bluntness at theta 70: b 1.17 (geometry margin 0.034), D 3.0, gamma -3.15. Tests the geometry edge and the benefit of very blunt noses.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.0,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.17,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.15},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":236000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the b-scaling of q and T near the buildable-geometry boundary; the cone is about 37 mm long, so a minimum-length rule could reject it.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1c570e52d539\",\"rationale\":\"Small-D, lower-bluntness point (D 2.5, theta 60, b 0.7) at gamma -3.1 to see how g and mass behave for a compact capsule.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.5,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.7,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":60.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":416000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":409,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extra coverage of the higher-q, higher-T part of the feasible set.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a6b969cef0a0\",\"rationale\":\"D 2.95, theta 66, b 0.9 (geometry margin 0.075), gamma -3.0: a low-risk sibling of the anchor with a slightly shallower entry for g margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":2.95,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Provides a robust feasible point in case the steeper siblings fail g.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-316c5e108e1a\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.05, theta 63, b 0.85 (geometry margin 0.060), gamma -3.25: near the mass-fraction ceiling with moderate bluntness.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.05,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.85,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":63.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":279000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the mass-fraction ceiling with a higher-theta shape than C-a6b969cef0a0, and adds T-focused coverage.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":286825,"type":"result","duration_ms":347218,"uuid":"7cae72a9-a268-4ebe-9ada-da6d15db84a5","ttft_stream_ms":1205,"time_to_request_ms":44,"first_content_frame_ms":1206,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
